# What is a Merge Conflict?

A merge conflict occurs when Git cannot automatically combine changes from two different lines of development.

For example:
main
  │
  A ─── B ─── C
           \
            D ─── E
                 ↑
              feature

If both branches modify the same part of a file differently, Git doesn't know which version you want.

Therefore:
Git
 ↓
Cannot automatically decide
 ↓
CONFLICT
 ↓
Human must resolve it

############# Complete Conflict Resolution Workflow ##########

The complete workflow is:

                 git merge
                     ↓
                  Conflict
                     ↓
                git status
                     ↓
             Find conflicted files
                     ↓
              Open the files
                     ↓
           Understand both changes
                     ↓
              Resolve manually
                     ↓
                 git add
                     ↓
               git commit
                     ↓
             Merge completed
